    "text": "A `Vec<T>` is an owned, growable vector on the heap. It owns its data and is the only way to have `T: !Clone` contents where you know you want multiple owners.\n\nA slice `&[T]` (or `&mut [T]`) is a view/cursor into memory that holds a pointer and a length. It is not owned. A `Vec` can be \"sliced\" by taking a reference to a range (`&[T]`).\n\nA `Vec` can be dynamic length, where you can push/pop, while a slice reference is fixed length. You can abstract over slices and work with vectors, arrays, and other container types the same way."
